## MONITORING MODE (Runs After Initial Setup)

After any of the 3 modes complete initial setup:

**Continuous Monitoring:**
```
System monitors code as developer writes:
  ↓
IF new APIs/services detected:
  ↓
  Check AGENT_MODE:
  
  If AGENT_MODE = true:
    → Auto-implement (workflow + activities + tests)
    → Show notification:
  "✅ Auto-implemented: [API name]
   📄 Tests: 15/15 passed
   📊 Priority: HIGH (score: 80)
   📁 Files: temporal/workflows/..., temporal/activities/..."
    → Update registry
  
  If AGENT_MODE = false:
    → Show prompt:
      "🔍 Detected: [API name] (suitable for Temporal)
       Priority: [HIGH/LOW]
       
       Implement Temporal for this? [Y/N]"
    → Wait for approval
    → If Y: Temporarily set AGENT_MODE = true → Implement → Ask about keeping mode ON/OFF
    → If N: Skip and continue monitoring
```

**Mode can be toggled anytime using commands:**
- "Enable agent mode" → Batch implement all HIGH priority → Ask to keep ON/OFF
- "Disable agent mode" → Switch to interactive prompts

